{%- comment -%}
  TIKVES LONDON . SITE CSS, IN THE HEAD
  28 Sep 2026, speed. Rendered from layout/theme.liquid at the end of the
  head, after the theme's own inline styles, so every rule below is in
  place before the page first paints.

  Until today these rules lived in two sections of the Footer group,
  tl-site-css and tikves-band-guard, and so arrived at the very end of the
  HTML, after the whole page. On a slow connection the age gate, the
  policy links and the home page bands could paint in the theme's own
  styling first and then change when the rules caught up. The rules are
  unchanged; only their place has moved. Both sections are gone from
  sections/footer-group.json, and their files were deleted on
  27 Oct 2026.

  Later position wins on equal specificity, so this snippet renders after
  css-variables, tikves-head-css, kit.overrides and the theme's inline
  style block. Section styles that print in the body (the age gate and
  the newsletter popup) target their own ids, so they win on specificity
  either way, exactly as before.

  ONE. Site-wide overrides. Link styling for policy pages and rich text,
  the footer in Paper Deep and Ink (operator ruling 13 Sep 2026; theme
  settings color_footer and color_footer_text still say Wine and Cream
  and settings_data.json is never written from a session, so the
  variables are overridden here), the age gate panel, and the newsletter
  popup as a centred stack. Popup rules are scoped on
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"], not on an id, because section
  ids inside section groups are generated by Shopify.

  TWO. Band alternation guard, added 7 Sep 2026. The home page alternates
  Paper and Paper Deep bands. When two tinted sections end up next to each
  other, by a change of order in the theme editor, the second drops back
  to Paper so the page keeps its rhythm. Banded sections: Top trending,
  By the bottle, Masters of Wine, Kumova rakija and the trust row; their
  ids all end in the section key.

  THREE. Policy pages as documents, operator ruling 2 Oct 2026. Every
  Shopify policy (/policies/...) and the policy-type pages listed below
  read like a document: title on the left, body in the text face, and
  section headings as short bold lines in the text face, not large serif
  headings. Reference the operator gave: a plain return-policy page with
  a left title and bold run-in subheadings. Rendered only on those pages.
  The page header carries the theme's text-center class, which is
  !important in Impulse, so the left alignment has to be !important too.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  .shopify-policy__body a,
  main .rte a,
  #MainContent .rte a,
  .shopify-policy__container a {
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------- */
  /* Footer. Paper Deep ground, Ink text.            */
  /* Operator ruling 13 Sep 2026: Wine off the       */
  /* footer. Theme settings color_footer and         */
  /* color_footer_text still say Wine and Cream;     */
  /* settings_data.json is never written from a      */
  /* session, so the variables are overridden here.  */
  /* The email field is styled in                    */
  /* snippets/footer-newsletter.liquid.              */
  /* ---------------------------------------------- */

  :root {
    --colorFooter: #F6EEE8;
    --colorFooterText: #1F2328;
    --colorFooterTextAlpha01: #1F2328;
    --urlIcoSelectFooter: var(--urlIcoSelect);
  }

  .site-footer {
    background-color: #F6EEE8;
    color: #1F2328;
  }

  .site-footer a,
  .site-footer .footer__title,
  .site-footer h4,
  .site-footer p,
  .site-footer .rte {
    color: #1F2328;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------- */
  /* Age gate. Cream panel on a plain dark backdrop. */
  /* No photograph, so nothing to download first.    */
  /* Impulse paints the backdrop from several        */
  /* elements, so all of them are covered here.      */
  /* ---------------------------------------------- */

  age-verification-popup.age-verification-popup--image-false,
  .age-verification-popup.age-verification-popup--image-false,
  .age-verification-popup.age-verification-popup--image-false .modal__inner,
  .age-verification-popup.age-verification-popup--image-false .modal__centered {
    background-color: {{ settings.color_header }} !important;
  }

  .age-verification-popup.age-verification-popup--image-false .modal__centered-content {
    background-color: {{ settings.color_body_bg }} !important;
    max-width: 460px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .age-verification-popup .modal__centered-content--padded {
    padding-top: 26px;
  }

  .age-verification-popup .tl-gate-logo img {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .age-verification-popup .age-verification-popup__content h2,
  .age-verification-popup .age-verification-popup__decline-content h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------- */
  /* Newsletter popup. Centred stack, mobile first.  */
  /* Headline stays in the heading serif.           */
  /* Hierarchy is a sandwich: small, huge, small.    */
  /* ---------------------------------------------- */

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter-popup__content {
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Logo sits on its own. Gap below is a theme setting. */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-logo {
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-logo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-rule {
    display: block;
    width: 56px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 20px auto 0;
    background: {{ settings.color_borders }};
  }

  /* Headline. Lines 1 and 3 match. */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-head {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-head span {
    display: block;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-small,
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-sub {
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-big {
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: {{ settings.color_button }};
    margin: 10px 0 8px;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter-popup__content .rte p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  /* Stack the form instead of input beside button */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .popup-cta {
    margin: 0;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .input-group {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .input-group-field,
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .input-group-btn {
    display: block;
    float: none;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter__input {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    text-align: left;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid {{ settings.color_body_text }};
    font-size: 16px;
    padding: 17px 16px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .input-group-btn .btn {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    font-size: 15px;
    padding-top: 19px;
    padding-bottom: 19px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  /* Fine print under the button */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .tl-pop-fine {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* Kill the inherited gap between the panel and the dismiss link */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter,
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter-popup {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__centered-content {
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    padding-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  /* Close control reads as a small text link at the foot */
  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__close {
    position: static;
    display: block;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    margin: 14px auto 0;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__close .icon-close {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__close:after {
    content: "No thanks";
    font-size: 14px;
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: {{ settings.color_body_text }};
  }

  /* Panel hugs its content instead of filling the screen */
  @media only screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter-popup__image-wrapper {
      display: none;
    }

    [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__inner {
      display: flex !important;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 100%;
      padding: 16px;
    }

    [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__centered {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 460px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      height: auto !important;
      min-height: 0 !important;
      padding-bottom: 22px;
    }

    [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .modal__centered-content {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto !important;
      max-height: none !important;
    }

    [data-section-type="newsletter-popup"] .newsletter-popup__content {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 26px 20px 18px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% style %}
  [id$="__ladder"] + [id$="__singles"],
  [id$="__ladder"] + [id$="__mw_voices"],
  [id$="__ladder"] + [id$="__tk_kumova"],
  [id$="__ladder"] + [id$="__trust"],

  [id$="__singles"] + [id$="__ladder"],
  [id$="__singles"] + [id$="__mw_voices"],
  [id$="__singles"] + [id$="__tk_kumova"],
  [id$="__singles"] + [id$="__trust"],

  [id$="__mw_voices"] + [id$="__ladder"],
  [id$="__mw_voices"] + [id$="__singles"],
  [id$="__mw_voices"] + [id$="__tk_kumova"],
  [id$="__mw_voices"] + [id$="__trust"],

  [id$="__tk_kumova"] + [id$="__ladder"],
  [id$="__tk_kumova"] + [id$="__singles"],
  [id$="__tk_kumova"] + [id$="__mw_voices"],
  [id$="__tk_kumova"] + [id$="__trust"],

  [id$="__trust"] + [id$="__ladder"],
  [id$="__trust"] + [id$="__singles"],
  [id$="__trust"] + [id$="__mw_voices"],
  [id$="__trust"] + [id$="__tk_kumova"] {
    background-color: #F6EEE8 !important;
  }

  /* The Masters block paints its own background from its settings, so
     it needs the inner element covering as well. */
  [id$="__ladder"] + [id$="__mw_voices"] .tkv,
  [id$="__singles"] + [id$="__mw_voices"] .tkv,
  [id$="__tk_kumova"] + [id$="__mw_voices"] .tkv,
  [id$="__trust"] + [id$="__mw_voices"] .tkv {
    background-color: #F6EEE8 !important;
  }
{% endstyle %}

{%- liquid
  assign tl_policy_doc = false
  if request.page_type == 'policy'
    assign tl_policy_doc = true
  elsif request.page_type == 'page'
    assign tl_policy_handles = 'delivery,returns,cookie-policy,age-verification,accessibility,terms-of-service' | split: ','
    if tl_policy_handles contains page.handle
      assign tl_policy_doc = true
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if tl_policy_doc -%}
{% style %}
  /* THREE. Policy pages as documents. Title left, same size as every other
     page title. Section headings are short bold lines in the text face,
     sitting close to the paragraph they introduce. */
  .template-page .section-header,
  .template-page .section-header.text-center,
  .template-page .section-header__title,
  .shopify-policy__title,
  .shopify-policy__title h1 {
    text-align: left !important;
  }

  main .rte h2,
  .shopify-policy__body h2 {
    font-family: var(--typeBasePrimary), var(--typeBaseFallback);
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    margin: 28px 0 6px;
  }

  main .rte h3,
  .shopify-policy__body h3 {
    font-family: var(--typeBasePrimary), var(--typeBaseFallback);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    margin: 20px 0 4px;
  }

  main .rte p,
  main .rte li,
  .shopify-policy__body p,
  .shopify-policy__body li {
    text-align: left;
  }

  @media only screen and (min-width: 769px) {
    main .rte h2,
    .shopify-policy__body h2 {
      font-size: 18px;
      margin-top: 32px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}
{%- endif -%}